        <section id="case-study"  class="t-bg-primary1a i-casestudy">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Case study
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <h3>Case study - How people become backend developers</h3>
<p>To be a backend developer, it is often a requirement to have a bachelor’s degree in computer science or another closely related field, and have often worked in a more junior role before they start. Backend developers must have a good technological skills, and are often well-versed in several different programming languages.</p>
<p>As the job involves a lot of problem solving, this job role fits someone who is methodological and enjoys logical challenges.</p>
<p>Another good reason for choosing the role is that it pays well.</p>
<p>The work can be very fulfilling, and developers are constantly updating their knowledge/learning new skills. However, work often overruns outside of normal hours, or have to get taken home because of problems which arise as you are working/do not get resolved before the end of the work day.</p>
<p>Please see the below interview to learn more about this role.</p>

      </div>
